    <h2>FAQ<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <details><summary>What is the safe code in The Game Night Agency?</summary><p><b>55793</b>. The keypad takes five digits and that is the number written on the crumpled note from the bottom shelf of the game shelf.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Where do you find the code in Level 7?</summary><p>On the bottom shelf of the board-game shelf, next to the Scrabble box: a small white crumpled scrap you can pick up at 7:13. Smooth it out in your inventory and it reads 5-5-7-9-3. It is not in the drawer and it is not on the letter notes.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is the checkerboard a chess puzzle?</summary><p>No. It is a packing puzzle: loose pieces with a checkerboard pattern are dragged into the recessed board until the pattern closes. There is no legal-move rule and no chess opening to spot.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Do the letter notes open the safe?</summary><p>No. The six notes carry letter pairs. H=C, T=B, M=T, G=Q, N=M, I=S. And the keypad only takes digits. The safe code comes from the crumpled paper. The notes belong to the Game Night neon sign, where only some letters glow.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How long does Level 7 take?</summary><p>Our recording finishes with an in-game time of <b>7:37</b> and a reward of <b>+50 coins</b>. A first run takes longer, because both floors have to be searched before the odd little scrap on the game shelf means anything.</p></details>

